          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Looks well; no acute distress."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-7",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-7",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Right index finger lesion examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Dorsolateral aspect just distal to the PIP joint: approximately 5–6 mm red, friable dome-shaped papule on a narrow stalk with a moist surface. Mild bleeding on light contact during examination, settling with direct pressure."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-8",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-8",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Right index finger surrounding findings"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "No surrounding erythema, warmth, induration, or pus."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-9",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-9",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Right hand and index finger function"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Grip strength within normal limits bilaterally; able to make a full fist and open the hand against resistance. Fine motor function intact; able to fast finger tap, count coins, and simulate till use without difficulty. Full active and passive range of motion at the right index finger PIP, DIP, and MCP joints without pain. Sensation intact, capillary refill normal, and hand function preserved."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-10",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-10",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Gait and stance"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Independent gait with normal pattern and stable stance; able to fully weight bear. No issues noted while walking to the door."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-11",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-11",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Reported right index finger lesion symptoms and impact"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Lesion noticed approximately 4–5 weeks after a box-cutter nick. Small red lump that bleeds easily with minor trauma, especially when using the till or handling notes. Irritating and a nuisance rather than painful; recurrent bleeding affects cash handling and stock work and requires stopping to apply bandages."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-12",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-12",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Associated reported symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Reports no fevers, spreading redness, reduced hand range of motion, or other skin lesions."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-13",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-13",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Right index finger lesion red-flag findings"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "No pigment, atypical borders, lymph nodes, or systemic symptoms reported or noted today."
      }
    },
